# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Built binaries (rooted so a package named grpctui/ is never ignored)
/grpctui
/cmd/grpctui/grpctui

# GoReleaser build output
/dist/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
!**/testdata/**/*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Runtime logs and state (zap writes to a file; see CLAUDE.md)
*.log
/grpctui.log

# TLS material — never commit client certs or private keys (v0.4 mTLS).
# Test fixtures under testdata/ are exempt: they must be committed for tests to run.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
!**/testdata/**/*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.crt

# AI/agent tooling — deliberately not part of the published repo.
# NOTE: CLAUDE.md is ignored, so a fresh clone carries no project conventions.
# Keep this file in sync manually across machines, or drop it from this list.
# Rooted (/) so a Go package named agent/ or claude/ deeper in the tree is unaffected.
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/
/.agents/
/agent/
/skills-lock.json
/.mcp.json

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
